From 30e9f2269adb12829ab2a313e0ac63c2c95eac8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:56:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] jm-v7 014: Bifrost tessellation

tessellationShader and extendedDynamicState2PatchControlPoints on v6/v7,
with the v9 tessellation limits. PANVK_DEBUG=no_tess turns them off.
A tessellated draw is recorded as two draws in one job chain
(panvk_tess_draw()):

1. The vertex shader over the API draw, compiled for clip space when a
   tess control shader follows and linked with every generic slot kept.
   Its tiler job is replaced by the tess control job: the TCS is
   compiled as compute (panvk_nir_lower_tcs_inputs() from 007, then
   poly_nir_lower_tcs() and panvk_nir_lower_tess_params()), one
   workgroup per patch and instance, one invocation per output vertex.
   New panlib_v7_tess_setup sizes it from the draw's command (written on
   the CPU for vkCmdDraw), a NULL job without patches.
2. The libpoly tessellator as new v6/v7 libpan kernels:
   panlib_v7_tessellate (COUNT), panlib_v7_tess_prefix (serial, one
   thread: the 1024-wide panlib_prefix_sum_tess is not used) and
   panlib_v7_tessellate (WITH_COUNTS, with the ccw swap). The prefix sum
   keeps the whole patches that fit 2^20 indices and the indirect
   varying buffer, and writes a VkDrawIndirectCommand.
3. That indirect draw, with the TES as its vertex shader
   (poly_nir_lower_tes(to_hw_vs), vertex i loads raw id index_buffer[i],
   the tess params come from a new graphics sysval). It is a normal JM
   indirect draw, so layers, views, the geometry emulation after the TES
   and transform feedback (passthrough built from the TES) apply as for
   any vertex shader.

Every tess kernel is a barrier job; the TCS output, counts and
tessellator output share one 64 MB device arena (allocated only when
tessellationShader is enabled). No CPU readback: direct, indexed,
indirect, multi-draw and byte-count draws take the same path. TCS/TES
are saved across meta operations. panvk_nir_tes_to_gs() (007, unused by
this design) is removed, and per-vertex inputs with a dynamic array index
now look the slot up at run time.

Limits: 8192 patches per draw (less with large TCS outputs), 2^20
indices, 8192 primitives into a GS or XFB; whole patches past them are
dropped (direct draws log once). FS gl_PrimitiveID without a GS is the
tiler primitive index. Points draw at size 1. v9+ is unchanged.

Build-tested, and recorded/submitted under the panfrost drm-shim on a
host debug build (see the README); no Bifrost device run. biblioklept

